{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786993884,"nonce":"91UY9XEolSq93/8EGIGZ95/RXq8=","title":"The notification path decides whether to be quiet by reading a denormalised timestamp, not `alert_snoozes`","message":"**What is wrong.** Whether oto speaks is decided against a projection. The suppression path\nreads `alerts.snoozed_until` — a bare timestamp maintained by a second write path — while the\nauthoritative row, which knows who silenced it, why, and how it ended, is never consulted.\n\n**The demonstration.** `internal/notification/repository/snapshot.go` selects\n`a.snoozed_until` from `alerts` at `:110` and `:129`, counts snoozed members with\n`count(*) FILTER (WHERE a.snoozed_until IS NOT NULL AND a.snoozed_until \u003e $3)` at `:120`, and\nbuilds `snap.SnoozedAlerts` from it at `:505` and `:536`.\n\n`db/migrations/00017_snooze.sql:24-27` says the split was deliberate and which side is\nauthoritative: \"A SEPARATE TABLE, DELIBERATELY. Putting `snoozed_by` / `snooze_note` on\n`alerts` […] gives snooze history for free. `alerts.snoozed_until` is a bare timestamp.\" The\nprojection is kept in step by `writeSnoozeProjection`, called from\n`internal/alerts/service/actions.go:448` (start) and `:523` (end).\n\nThe cost of reading the authoritative table is small, and the index says so:\n`alert_snoozes_active_idx` is `UNIQUE (alert_id) WHERE ended_at IS NULL`\n(`00017_snooze.sql:72`), so it holds only currently-active snoozes — dozens of rows, not\nmillions. A left join against that hashes the small side and streams the members past it,\nwhether a group holds five or five thousand.\n\nOn the UI side the projection's whole remaining justification is one base-table predicate at\n`internal/alerts/repository/alert.go:682` plus a badge, and both disappear under a Quiet tab.\n\n**Why it matters.** `internal/notification/repository/events.go:171-172` states a requirement\nthe projection cannot serve: \"When a signal is snoozed AND throttled AND the channel is quiet,\nan operator who unsnoozes and still hears nothing needs to already know why.\" A bare timestamp\ncannot name the person, the note or the `ended_reason`; the authoritative row carries all\nthree. Reading it also narrows a cross-module SQL dependency from `alerts` — wide, hot,\nfrequently changed — to a single-concept table.\n\nSeparately, the 30-day maximum means a user can be blind for a month with nothing on screen to\nremind them. There is no surface listing what is currently quiet, so a snooze becomes permanent\nby forgetfulness.\n\n**Where.** `internal/notification/repository/snapshot.go:110, 120, 129, 505, 536, 649`;\n`internal/alerts/repository/alert.go:42, 60, 71, 131, 682, 843, 1067`;\n`internal/alerts/service/actions.go:139, 448, 523, 597-602`;\n`db/migrations/00017_snooze.sql:68-78, 98`;\n`web/src/features/alerts/filters.ts:75-82, 99, 139, 156, 206-217, 241, 295`.\n\n**Scope.** medium\n\n**Done when.** Every suppression decision reads `alert_snoozes`. No module outside the `alerts`\nread path references `snoozed_until`, and an arch test refuses the column's reintroduction.\n`alerts.snoozed_until`, `alerts_snooze_idx` and `writeSnoozeProjection` are gone. A new partial\nindex `alert_snoozes (org_id, snoozed_until) WHERE ended_at IS NULL` serves the tab, its count\nand the anti-join's build side — neither existing index leads with `org_id`.\n\nThe alert list has two tabs. The main tab excludes snoozed alerts via a left anti-join; a\n**Quiet** tab drives from `alert_snoozes` into `alerts` by primary key and carries the same\nthree group-by axes. The tab is present even at zero, its count hidden at zero, and the badge\ncarries the worst state inside it — `Quiet (12 · 2 firing)`, not `Quiet (12)` — because that\nbadge is now the only signal that something live is hidden. Snoozing from the main list says\nwhere the row went. The roll-up's `snoozed` counter is dropped: the roll-up shares the list's\nfilter, so the number would always be zero.\n\nThis reverses `web/src/features/alerts/filters.ts:78-80` — \"hiding snoozed alerts from the\ndefault list is how an incident is lost\" — and the reversal is recorded next to that comment in\nthe repo's usual form: a badge on row 400 of a scrolling list is already invisible, whereas a\nlabelled tab whose count carries severity is not.","files":null}]}